            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Tn4Ch",
              "name": "A run starts from a request: a workflow ",
              "context": "p",
              "fill": "#d9d9df",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "height": 153.56,
              "content": "A run starts from a request: a workflow with its params, or a process on an agent, with --continue or --reuse naming an earlier run. Resolve turns it into definitions or a refusal. The composition plans every step, those in branch arms a run may not take included, and lists what this Agister does not run yet; a refusal of either kind ends the command before anything runs and before any record. agister check shares that list, so it refuses exactly what a run would.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "Helvetica Neue",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "z5mODL",
