                          "name": "Caption",
                          "fill": "$text-dim",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "An arrow is a call through a port; the composition, in cmd/agister, wires every one. Core knows no settings file, no git and no runtime: it is given a workflow of items and a caller, and tells what happens to an events port.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.65,
                          "fontFamily": "$sans",
                          "fontSize": 14,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "yXTAq",
                      "name": "P request",
                      "fill": "$text-body",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A run starts from a request: a workflow with its params, or a process on an agent, with --continue or --reuse naming an earlier run. Resolve turns it into definitions or a refusal. The composition plans every step, those in branch arms a run may not take included, and lists what this Agister does not run yet. A refusal of either kind ends the command before anything runs and before any record.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.65,
                      "fontFamily": "$sans",
                      "fontSize": 16,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "uA1RH",
                      "name": "Callout check",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "fill": "#F28DB012",
                      "stroke": "$workflow",
                      "strokeWidth": {
                        "left": 2
